{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runpod/runpodctl/pulls/330","id":4369037787,"node_id":"PR_kwDOHHW5XM8AAAABBGo52w","html_url":"https://github.com/runpod/runpodctl/pull/330","diff_url":"https://github.com/runpod/runpodctl/pull/330.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/runpod/runpodctl/pull/330.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runpod/runpodctl/issues/330","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runpod/runpodctl/pulls/330/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runpod/runpodctl/pulls/330/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runpod/runpodctl/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runpod/runpodctl/issues/330/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runpod/runpodctl/statuses/d38156399b795c488059ea3aa7d8f450feddcc27","number":330,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(pod): remove --stop-after and --terminate-after","user":{"login":"justinwlin","id":15874969,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1ODc0OTY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15874969?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinwlin","html_url":"https://github.com/justinwlin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinwlin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinwlin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinwlin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinwlin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinwlin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinwlin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinwlin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinwlin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinwlin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`--stop-after` and `--terminate-after` never worked. Both are removed.\n\nPart of CON-1258, which stays open: this removes the broken surface, it does not fix the feature. runpod/RunPod#5718 is the backend fix that makes the deadline actually fire, and runpodctl#331 restores the flags with validation once it lands.\n\n## Why\n\nThe flags were forwarded to `podFindAndDeployOnDemand` as `stopAfter` / `terminateAfter`. The API accepts both as valid input and then does not act on them: the pod keeps running, and billing, past the deadline.\n\nThe value is also write-only. It is not readable on the `Pod` type and does not exist in REST v2 at all, so the CLI cannot confirm the timer landed, and cannot detect afterwards that it did not fire.\n\nThree further problems, all moot once the flag is gone:\n\n- CPU pods dropped it silently — they are created over REST v2, which has no scheduling field.\n- Past timestamps were accepted; the deadline simply never arrived.\n- The documented duration form (`1h`, `24h`, `7d`) was rejected by the GraphQL `DateTime` scalar, leaking the raw scalar error. Only RFC 3339 was ever sent successfully.\n\nNothing a client can do makes the timer fire, and a flag that silently costs money is worse than no flag.\n\n## What changed\n\nBoth flags are deleted. Passing one is a usage error:\n\n```\n$ runpodctl pod create --image ubuntu:22.04 --stop-after 2h\n{\"error\":\"unknown flag: --stop-after\",\"code\":\"usage_error\"}\n```\n\nThey no longer appear in `--help` or the generated docs, and `StopAfter` / `TerminateAfter` are dropped from `CreatePodGQLInput`. `internal/duration` is untouched — `duration.Parse` still backs `--since` and `--wait-timeout`.\n\n## Release notes\n\n**Breaking.** `runpodctl pod create --stop-after` and `--terminate-after` are removed. Scripts passing either now fail with `unknown flag` and a non-zero exit instead of creating a pod on a timer that never fired. There is no replacement until the backend enforces the deadline; until then, stop or terminate the pod explicitly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence</summary>\n\nTwo GPU pods created against production with `stopAfter` roughly four minutes out. Both stayed `RUNNING` past the deadline, with no state change and no error. Deleted manually afterwards.\n\n| Pod | stopAfter | Last observation | desiredStatus |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `mqb8yey2sq8qka` | 16:45:46Z | 16:49:34Z | `RUNNING` |\n| `bdwcl5lzqwqny0` | 16:48:35Z | 16:49:34Z | `RUNNING` |\n\n`go build ./...` and `go test ./...` green.\n</details>","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-26T16:46:13Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T22:51:25Z","closed_at":"2026-08-27T22:51:22Z","merged_at":"2026-08-27T22:51:22Z","merge_commit_sha":"51ca7f02ab5cb57c09ad917172af36c29a58790c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"runpod:justinlin/con-1258-enforce-runpodctl-stop-after-and-terminate-after-timers","ref":"justinlin/con-1258-enforce-runpodctl-stop-after-and-terminate-after-timers","repo":{"id":477477212,"node_id":"R_kgDOHHW5XA","name":"runpodctl","full_name":"runpod/runpodctl","owner":{"login":"runpod","id":95939477,"node_id":"O_kgDOBbfrlQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95939477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/runpod","html_url":"https://github.com/runpod","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runpod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runpod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runpod/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runpod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runpod/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runpod/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runpod/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runpod/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runpod/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false